{"kind":"request","text":"EK-1: the standing value check of Explore, in `packages/derive`.\n\nThe owner approved this exception on 16 November 2026. It is the\nsecond exception of the form of the E1 export (`docs/kernel.md`\nsection 7). Audit `425637e6` found the need, and act `d038a2ee`\nitem 2 holds the shape.\n\nWork:\n1. One pure value check in `packages/derive/src/grant.ts`, shared\n   with `judgeGrant`. It keeps the present order: membership, key\n   and revocation first, the guards of the use next, the other\n   value checks last.\n2. One grant value for the body of the judge with no `fresh`, and\n   with `issued` at the actual membership head. Each row of\n   `observes` stays `unavailable` under that value.\n3. `Grant` of the contract, the runtime, the replay and\n   `predictionGrant` do not change.\n\nThis request holds no client code, no source of the standing and no\nMCP change. Steps E2 and E3 use the split after my ruling on the\nsource.","body":{"conditions":"The runtime and the replay give unchanged answers on the corpus, as the E1 export proved. judgeGrant keeps its precedence, and one test pins the order of its refusals before and after the split. No caller gets a grant with no fresh except the body input of Explore, and a type or a test shows that the runtime and the replay refuse it. docs/kernel.md section 7 records the exception with the owner's date. A short design proposal comes before source. Side lane: it takes a gate position after AE-1 and C4.","target_head":"6728059211cee75dc0f6fdd104ef52a44c5f7da0","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}